PARITY NOTES (web → native, no shortcuts)
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
• States: loading→TSSkeleton, empty→ContentUnavailableView("Send a request to see the response"),
  loaded→FadeIn(status bar + body + collapsible headers); status styling success<300 / redirect<400 / error≥400
  (statusSuccess/statusWarning/statusDanger @ bg/10 + border/20). History strip hidden when empty.
• Body: contentType.includes("json") ⇒ JSONSerialization pretty-print (object/array only, like
  JSON.stringify(_,null,2) over a non-string body); otherwise raw bodyText. Unparseable JSON ⇒ raw fallback.
• Snippets: generateSnippet ported byte-for-byte — cURL auth note + ` \`+NL joins, JS headers/body block,
  python json= arg + method.toLowerCase(), Go GET special-case + `body ?? "{}"`; body-gate = non-empty && method≠GET.
• SnippetPanel: language picker (cURL/JavaScript/Python/Go) + labelled Copy (clipboard seam, Copy⇄✓).
  NOTE: SwiftUI View.body collision — stored prop renamed `requestBody`; public init label stays `body:` for parity
  (caught RED by G1, fixed; same gotcha the prior accepted run recorded).
• i18n: all 6 web keys via the per-surface "ResponseViewer" table (value: web English fallback); zero literals.
• a11y: VoiceOver labels on every control (chips carry "{method} {path} → {status} ({ms}ms)"), disclosure
  expanded/collapsed announced, body value exposed, Reduce-Motion-aware chevron, Dynamic Type via tokens.
• Telemetry: .task → ResponseViewerSurface.reportOpen → view.opened surface=ResponseViewer (redaction-safe os_log).

